d parties when you browse ACU’s website. ACU’s website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages with whom we share information about your use of our site, for example our social media, advertising and analytics partners who may personalise advertisements to you on third party websites. These third parties can be located overseas, including the USA, Ireland, UK and the Netherlands. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the Cookie Declaration on our website. Learn more about how we manage personal information, how you may access and correct your personal information, how you can complain about a breach of privacy and how you can contact us, in our Privacy Policy . Do not sell or share my personal information Allow all cookies Customize Allow selection Use necessary cookies only Skip to content Study at ACU Study at ACU Find a course New courses ACU Online Short courses Course types explained Course guides Core Curriculum Why study at ACU How to apply Undergraduate students Postgraduate students Short courses and individual units Entry programs and pathways Find your pathway or entry program I have completed military service I am Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander I am a first responder Undergraduate study at ACU Non School Leavers at ACU Postgraduate study at ACU International study at ACU Research study at ACU Study overseas Fees and scholarships Domestic student fees International student fees Scholarships Financing your studies Responding to an offer Accept your offer and enrol Orientation Defer your offer or withdraw Credit and prior learning Leadership academy Important dates Future students events Career advisors How parents can help Faith and Values Student forms ACU Guarantee applications are now open - closing 14 September 2026. International students International students ACU中文官网 Access International Course Guide online Download student guides Student and alumni stories International student scholarships How to apply Study undergraduate Study postgraduate Study research Study English Pathway programs Diploma programs Tertiary Preparation Program (Health Sciences) Study abroad and exchange Semester programs Gateway to ACU Arriving and living in Australia Accommodation options Student visas International student fees Find an ACU-approved agent Meet ACU in your country International partners Contact us - ACU International All you need to know about international student life at ACU Student life Student life Experience uni before you start Experience ACU Explore your local campus Open Day Student stories ACU Thrive Campus facilities Food, drink and recreation facilities Learning and teaching facilities Sports, health and wellbeing facilities Student safety Student services Academic skills development Campus ministry Career development services Connect2Uni First year students Counselling services Disability support Medical centres Student advocacy Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander student services Student Veterans Support Program Library Clubs, activities and student associations Student associations Clubs and societies Creative and cultural activities Leadership opportunities ACU Sport Gyms, fitness classes and facilities Sports clubs and activities UniSport Social sport and sport facililties Elite Athlete and Performer Program Gain work experience Student accommodation Rental Advisory Service Student Accommodation Scholarships Graduation Locations Locations Ballarat Blacktown Brisbane Canberra Melbourne North Sydney Rome Strathfield Townsville Leadership Centre Co-Lab business incubator ACU Sport facilities Community event spaces and venue hire The Gaudete Centre, Brisbane The Greg Craven Centre, Melbourne The Peter Cosgrove Centre, North Sydney The Veritas Building Strathfield STEM Centre of Education Excellence Discovery Centre Everything you need in one place to help make your choice. Research and enterprise Research and enterprise Research expertise Find an expert Institutes and centres Faculties and schools Research facilities and capabilities Library Collaborate with ACU Innovate and research Join us on campus Connect with students Engage our candidates Graduate research Research degrees How to apply Find a scholarship Join a research project Meet our supervisors Why research at ACU Support and resources Research Enterprise Researcher development Graduate research Research supervision Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research and Enterprise) Graduate Research School Research vision 2033 Our focus Core themes Strategic priorities Contact us Find a research supervisor About ACU About ACU Reputation and ranking Vision 2033 Vision 2033 Plans Leadership and governance Organisational structure Government and public policy Vice-Chancellor and President Faith and Values What if I'm not Catholic? Community giving Community engagement Community-initiated research Sustainability at ACU News Events Careers at ACU Arts and culture hub Widening participation Employers and industry Our partnerships Research partners Publications Handbook by year First Peoples Directorate Empowering veterans Student veteran services Policies and procedures Professional Standards and Integrity Search Faculties, directorates and staff Faculty of Education and Arts Faculty of Health Sciences Faculty of Law and Business Faculty of Theology and Philosophy Directorates Institutes, academies and centres Search Search Search by keyword, course.. Show Me Everything Everything Courses Researcher Search Faith and Values Industry Alumni Giving to ACU Safety at ACU Current students Library Staff Contact us Search by keyword, course.. Show Me Everything Courses Researcher Search Search Menu ☰ Close X Home > Student life > Student services > Careers and Employability Career development and employability services Start your career while you study. As an ACU student, you'll be able to access a range of career development programs, events and support services to enhance your employability. There are many things you can do  during your time at university to improve your chances of successfully gaining  employment. ACU graduates can access careers support up to two years  post-completion of studies. Key services ACU CareerHub , an  online portal which provides students job opportunities, appointment bookings  and event information. Graduate Employment, our ACU Career Directory gives you exclusive access to graduate jobs, internships, career advice and reviews tailored to your study area. Application Assist is a step by step  process to enable students to build professional and competitive job  application documents. Learning the process of developing your resume,  addressing selection criteria and writing cover letters. Through this process,  access resources linking you to job search strategies and program information,  submit your application for review and register for professional development  workshops. The Careers and Employability provides appointments and online career advice, workshops and programs, employer events and connection Student Jobs on Campus (SJC) provides students with the opportunity to undertake paid employment across ACU campuses while completing their studies. Further information To learn more about other work experience opportunities at ACU, including student jobs on campus, visit our work experience page. Gain work experience Back to previous page Have a question? We're available 9am–5pm AEST, Monday to Friday If you’ve got a question, our AskACU team has you covered. You can search FAQs, email, live chat, call – whatever works for you. Live chat with us now Chat to our team for real-time answers to your questions. Launch live chat Visit our FAQs page Find answers to some commonly asked questions. See our FAQs Ask a question Call 1300 275 228 About ACU Faith and Values Working at ACU Giving to ACU Contact us Our campuses Ballarat Blacktown Brisbane Canberra Melbourne North Sydney Rome Strathfield ACU Online Connect with us Study online with us Still have questions? Accessibility Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Safety Copyright ©Australian Catholic University 1998-2026 ABN 15050192660 Provider Number PRV12008 CRICOS Reg 00004G Australian Catholic University acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands on which we live and work, and we pay our respects to Elders both past and present."
